@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #526B7B
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EDF4FB
skinparam stateBorderColor #526B7B
skinparam stateStartColor #163E52
skinparam stateEndColor #163E52
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3DF
skinparam noteBorderColor #B99557
skinparam nodesep 38
skinparam ranksep 48
hide empty description
top to bottom direction

title SM-M16 — User-managed record retention and actual reclamation
state "Active record/content\ncontext" as Active
state "Archived; retained under\npolicy" as Archived
state "Deletion requested /\nretained trash" as Trashed
state "Eligible reclamation\nconfirmed" as Reclaimed
[*] --> Active : scoped initial context
Active --> Archived : SM-T104 archive confirmed\n[authorized / confirmed]
Archived --> Active : SM-T105 restore visibility\n[eligible explicit restore]
Active --> Trashed : SM-T106 delete request confirmed\n[authorized / confirmed]
Archived --> Trashed : SM-T107 delete request confirmed\n[authorized / confirmed]
Trashed --> Active : SM-T108 restore retained item\n[retained / eligible /\nauthorized]
Trashed --> Reclaimed : SM-T109 reclamation confirmed\n[eligible / no protected refs]
legend bottom
A: accepted core behavior; P: existing proposal; R: proposed refinement.
State labels are analysis abstractions, not implemented enums.
Transition tables define full actor, guard, effect and status.
Unconfirmed operation effects require SM-M18 reconciliation.
endlegend
@enduml
